Decide whether two article clusters describe the SAME underlying real-world news event.

Use a strict standard:
- SAME means the same incident, attack, announcement, decision, or development on the same day.
- Different outlets, different casualty counts, or different damage details can still be SAME.
- Similar topic, same war, same country, repeated attacks on different cities, or different days are NOT SAME.
- If the evidence is too thin or ambiguous, choose same_event=false.

